From: hurrhnn <hurrhnn@icmp.kr>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 05:47:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: keep the inbound SOE context intact on submit

airoha_soe_submit_prepared_skb() clears ctx->tx.deferred_skb,
deferred_sa and deferred_dev for every context it submits. The tx and
rx members of struct airoha_soe_ctx share a union, and for an inbound
context these stores land on rx.saddr, rx.sport, rx.seq, rx.foe_hash and
rx.foe_valid. airoha_soe_complete_in() then hands a zero ESP sequence
number to xfrm_dev_packet_input_state_check(), whose replay check
rejects it, so with a replay window every inbound packet that completes
through the SOE CPU path is dropped. Without a replay window the NAT-T
check compares a zero source address and port with the SA, so every
ESP-in-UDP packet looks like a peer mapping change, calls
km_new_mapping() and disables the PPE path of the SA.

Only outbound contexts are ever deferred, so clear the deferral fields
for them alone. Inbound contexts keep the outer source address and
port, the ESP sequence number and the FOE metadata recorded by
airoha_soe_rx_plain_skb() until their completion.

Signed-off-by: hurrhnn <hurrhnn@icmp.kr>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_soe.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_soe.c
@@ -2391,9 +2391,11 @@ airoha_soe_submit_prepared_skb(struct ai
 		spin_unlock_bh(&sa->lock);
 		return err;
 	}
-	ctx->tx.deferred_skb = NULL;
-	ctx->tx.deferred_sa = NULL;
-	ctx->tx.deferred_dev = NULL;
+	if (ctx->dir == AIROHA_SOE_CTX_OUT) {
+		ctx->tx.deferred_skb = NULL;
+		ctx->tx.deferred_sa = NULL;
+		ctx->tx.deferred_dev = NULL;
+	}
 	if (untracked) {
 		/* A bound PPE entry consumes the SOE result instead of returning
 		 * it as a CPU completion. The bind barrier has already drained
